  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If we assume electron in hydrogen atom takes energy $12.09 \\mathrm{eV}$ from the incoming radiation, the maximum excited state of electron will be $n=3$. So, number of spectral lines is $\\frac{3(3-1)}{2}=3$.<br />Here we assume some part of energy $12.5 \\mathrm{eV}$ $-12.09 \\mathrm{eV}=0.41 \\mathrm{eV}$ get lost due to collision.",
    "image": null
